        "original_id": "acfc7b31-bb63-50c6-8ae1-426257eb5fad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: New York Islanders, New York Rangers, Pittsburgh Penguins, New Jersey Devils, WWE\n- Places: Madison Square Garden, New York City, New York metropolitan area\n- Events: 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, Survivor Series (2011)\n- Concepts: NHL franchises, pay-per-view events\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the New York Rangers in three games in the first round.\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders then defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games in the Quarter-finals after losing the first three games.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three NHL franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and New York Islanders.\n- Madison Square Garden is the home arena of the New York Rangers.\n- Madison Square Garden is also home to the New York Knicks and, since 1997, the New York Liberty.\n- Survivor Series (2011) was a WWE pay-per-view event held on November 20, 2011 at Madison Square Garden in New York City.",
